  "description": "Keys 1 to 3 control L1, L2, and the shutter by hand; the keys of L1 and L2 follow the status of their output, also after a scene. Keys 4 and 5 recall scenes 1 and 2 with a short press, and store them with a long press: each output then stores its current state as its value for that scene (DPT 18.001, learn bit). The switching actuator receives the scenes on one central scene object for its two outputs; the shutter actuator on the scene object of its output.",
